  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 305 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nThe upper-level trough slowly meanders over the forecast area on\nThursday before another upper low pinches over west and southwest\nTexas Thursday into Friday. A cold front will move through our\nregion during the day Thursday. Moisture will become more limited\nover our forecast area on Thursday behind the front, so convection\nif any should be isolated and mainly confined to far eastern \nparts of the forecast area ahead of the boundary. Isolated to \nscattered showers and storms may develop on Friday, with the \nbetter coverage confined to the higher terrain areas in the \nvicinity of the upper low. Surface high pressure builds into the\ncentral plains Friday and the resultant MSLP gradient may bring\nbreezy conditions to our region Friday. A brief period of high gap\nwinds will also be possible over the Guadalupe Mountains Thursday\nnight into Friday. Upper ridging builds back into the western U.S.\nthis weekend into early next week. Isolated to scattered showers/\nstorms should mainly remain confined over central and southern\nparts of our forecast area along the stalled boundary this weekend\ninto early next week. Temperatures will become more seasonal\nFriday through Monday with highs in the 70s and lows in the 50s to\nlower 60s.",
